{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מרכבות", :translit "merkhavot", :gloss "chariots"} {:he "ואת מרכבות השמש שרף באש", :translit "ve'et merkhavot ha-shamesh saraf ba-esh", :gloss "and the chariots of the sun he burned in fire"} {:he "מרכבות כבודך", :translit "merkhavot khivodekha", :gloss "chariots of Your glory"} {:he "מרכבות עמי נדיב", :translit "merkhavot ami nadiv", :gloss "chariots of My noble people"} {:he "רוכב שמים בעזרך", :translit "rokhev shamayim be-ezrekha", :gloss "Who rides the heavens with your help"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["מרכבות" "ואת מרכבות השמש שרף באש" "מרכבות כבודך" "מרכבות עמי נדיב"]}], :frame {:text "The burning of the sun-chariots by Josiah is recorded at 2 Kings 23:11. Shebna's attempt to ally with Sennacherib is described at Isaiah 22:15-19, where he is criticized for carving a lavish tomb, and Isaiah 36:3 records him as the official who went out to meet Sennacherib's forces. The phrase 'I do not know myself to be good' alludes to Proverbs 30:2, 'Surely I am more brutish than any man, and have not the understanding of a man.' The verse 'Who rides the heavens in your help' is Deuteronomy 33:26.", :sources ["2 Kings 23:11" "Isaiah 22:15-19" "Isaiah 36:3" "Proverbs 30:2" "Deuteronomy 33:26"]}} {:quotes [{:he "ומבחר", :translit "umivkhar", :gloss "and the choice"} {:he "ומבחר בחוריו ירדו לטבח", :translit "umivkhar bakhurav yaradu litavakh", :gloss "and the choice of his young men went down to the slaughter"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ומבחר" "ומבחר בחוריו ירדו לטבח"]}], :frame {:text "The second occurrence of 'and the choice' is at Isaiah 14:4, part of a taunt against the king of Babylon: 'the Lord has broken the staff of the wicked, the scepter of rulers, that struck the peoples in wrath with an unceasing stroke, that ruled the nations in anger with unrelenting persecution — the whole earth is at rest and quiet; they break forth into singing. The cypresses rejoice at you, the cedars of Lebanon, saying: Since you were laid low, no woodcutter comes up against us. Sheol beneath is stirred up to meet you when you come; it rouses the shades to greet you, all who were leaders of the earth; it raises from their thrones all who were kings of the nations — and the choice of his young men went down to the slaughter.' Ba'al HaTurim reads this descent to slaughter as the physical aftermath of drowning at the Red Sea, described in Exodus 15:5, 'the deeps cover them; they went down into the depths like a stone,' and Exodus 15:10, 'they sank like lead in the mighty waters.'", :sources ["Isaiah 14:4-19" "Exodus 15:5" "Exodus 15:10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 4, :occurrences ["מרכבות" "ואת מרכבות השמש שרף באש" "מרכבות כבודך" "מרכבות עמי נדיב"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "מרכבות", :refs ["2 Kings 23:11" "Isaiah 22:18" "Joel 2:5" "Zechariah 6:1" "Song of Songs 6:12" "1 Chronicles 4:31"], :n 6, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ואת מרכבות השמש שרף באש", :refs ["2 Kings 23:11"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מרכבות כבודך", :refs ["Isaiah 22:18"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "מרכבות עמי נדיב", :refs ["Song of Songs 6:12"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ומבחר" "ומבחר בחוריו ירדו לטבח"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "ומבחר", :refs ["Exodus 15:4" "Jeremiah 48:15"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:phrase "ומבחר בחוריו ירדו לטבח", :refs ["Jeremiah 48:15"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-13T00:33:14.483072381Z", :model "glm-5.2"}